  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "At Kugler Company, fertiliser businessman Mike Kugler joined his fellow leaders in advocating a local dealer network. Their message to farmers emphasised continuity at a time when mergers were reducing the choice of agricultural suppliers. Dealers who knew their communities could help growers plan fertiliser programmes, with their own businesses depending on those customers’ results.\n\nAway from the business, Kugler is a pilot who describes himself as comfortable with practical, hands-on work. He participates in aviation matters through local public service, serving on McCook’s Airport Advisory Commission and its Airport Zoning Board.",
    "html": "<p>At Kugler Company, fertiliser businessman Mike Kugler joined his fellow leaders in advocating a local dealer network. Their message to farmers emphasised continuity at a time when mergers were reducing the choice of agricultural suppliers. Dealers who knew their communities could help growers plan fertiliser programmes, with their own businesses depending on those customers’ results.</p>\r\n<p>Away from the business, Kugler is a pilot who describes himself as comfortable with practical, hands-on work. He participates in aviation matters through local public service, serving on McCook’s Airport Advisory Commission and its Airport Zoning Board.</p>\r\n",
    "word_count": 92,
